                <pb facs="0830" n="748" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg748"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 367.112 Er 4/11.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the American Minister in temporary charge of the Embassy at
                            Constantinople.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1911-02-28"><hi rendition="#italic">February 28,
                        1911</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>In view of the note from the Sublime Porte, dated January 2.1, 1911, transmitted
                    in your dispatch No. 310, of January 31, 1911, expressing regret and apology,
                    inform the foreign office that this Government is disposed to regard the
                    Erickson case as closed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Knox.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
